.Dd September 3, 2026
.Dt VDOTS-READ 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm vdots-read
.Nd read a Markdown file aloud (macOS say), headless
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -voice Ar V
.Op Fl -tone Ar warm Ns | Ns Ar clarity
.Op Fl -pace Ar follow Ns | Ns Ar relaxed Ns | Ns Ar natural
.Op Fl -rate Ar N
.Ar FILE.md
.Nm
.Brq Fl -export | Fl -publish | Fl -dry-run | Fl -sample | Fl -print-voice | Fl -print-pace
.Op ...
.Op Ar FILE.md
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the command-line path of the vdots read-aloud plugin: the same
Markdown parse, tech-pronunciation pass, and paced delivery as the in-editor
.Ic ;r
keymaps, driven by
.Xr nvim 1
in headless mode.
The rich in-editor experience \(em rendered preview pane, follow-along
highlight, pause / jump / resume-from-block, hardware media keys \(em lives in
.Pa lua/vdots/readaloud/ .
.Sh MODES
.Bl -tag -width "--print-voice"
.It Pq default
Speak
.Ar FILE
through
.Xr say 1 .
.It Fl -export
Render
.Pa <FILE>.m4a
and open it.
.It Fl -publish
Add to the listen library \(em forwards to
.Xr vdots-listen 1 Ic publish .
.It Fl -dry-run
Print the spoken script (with
.Ic [[slnc]]
pause markers), do not speak.
.It Fl -sample Op Ar FILE
Speak a short sample to audition a voice / pace.
.It Fl -print-voice Op Fl -tone Ar T
Print the voice that would be auto-picked.
.It Fl -print-pace Op Fl -pace Ar P
Print the resolved pace preset
.Pf ( Ic rate , Ic stretch , Ic say_rate ) .
.It Fl -transcript , Fl -cues Ar SECS , Fl -cues-json Ar SECS , Fl -chapters Ar SECS , Fl -meta , Fl -info
Bridge modes used by
.Xr vdots-listen 1 .
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width "--tone T"
.It Fl -voice Ar V
macOS voice name. Siri voices
.Pq e.g. Qq Siri Voice 4
are not auto-detected \(em pass them explicitly.
.It Fl -tone Ar warm Ns | Ns Ar clarity
Character used when auto-picking a voice. Default
.Ar warm .
.It Fl -clarity
Alias for
.Fl -tone Ar clarity .
.It Fl -pace Ar follow Ns | Ns Ar relaxed Ns | Ns Ar natural
Delivery preset. Default
.Ar follow .
.It Fl -rate Ar N
Override the preset's words-per-minute (pause lengths and time-stretch
unchanged).
.It Fl -lang Ar L
BCP-47 language tag for locale voice matching. Default
.Ar en-US .
.El
.Sh PACING
Every preset leaves a beat at clause marks, a longer rest at sentence ends,
and larger gaps between paragraphs / before headings. The unhurried feel
comes from a whole-file, pitch-preserving time-stretch applied after
.Xr say 1
renders
.Pf ( Xr rubberband 1 No if installed, else Xr ffmpeg 1 Ic atempo ) ;
inserting silence between every word was tried and removed \(em it sounded
like flash cards.
Tune in
.Pa lua/vdots/readaloud/pace.lua
.Pf ( Ic M.presets ) .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr rubberband 1 ,
.Xr say 1 ,
.Xr vdots 1 ,
.Xr vdots-listen 1 ,
.Xr vdots-publish 1
.Pp
.Ic :help vdots-readaloud
inside Neovim.
